{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>And it was very grievous to Moses.</b> He was distressed exceedingly." "<b>Do not turn to their offering.</b> According to its plain sense — the incense that they offer before you tomorrow, do not turn to it. And its midrash: he said, I know that they have a share in the public daily offerings — let their share too not be accepted before you for favor; let the fire leave it and not consume it (Tanchuma)." "<b>Not one donkey of theirs have I taken.</b> Not the donkey of one of them did I take. Even when I went from Midian to Egypt and mounted my wife and my sons on the donkey — and I could have taken that donkey from theirs, I did not take it but from my own. And the Targum renders ״שחרית״ — in Aramaic the king's angaria is thus called ״shachvar״."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:11:17.630023436Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}